From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:09:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 109/125] fix(formulas): declare [requires] formula_compiler
 instead of contract graph.v2 (gcp-hc5z.1)

gc doctor's formula-requirements check warns on every formula that still
uses the deprecated contract = "graph.v2" alias, which put 33 warnings on
every deacon patrol from this pack. Hunter ruled on gcp-hc5z to fix it
rather than wait on upstream, whose main has not migrated.

All 34 gascity/formulas/*.formula.toml files drop the contract line and
declare the table the gastown pack already uses:

    [requires]
    formula_compiler = ">=2.0.0"

The table goes immediately before each file's first table header, not
where the contract line was: in files like build-basic the contract line
is followed by top-level extends and target_required, and a header above
them would have moved those keys into [requires]. Each file was checked
with tomllib: the parsed document equals the original minus contract plus
the requires table. Every file declares it directly, without relying on
extends.

gc treats the two forms the same: both yield a >=2.0.0 compiler
constraint, and the compiler stamps gc.kind=workflow and
gc.formula_contract=graph.v2 on the root either way, so runtime root
checks are unchanged.

Tests: the four assertions that read gascity-pack formulas now require no
contract key and an exact requires table. resolve_formula and
resolve_formula_from_dirs merge contract and requires the same way (the
child's value wins, otherwise the first parent that has one). They set a
key only when some formula in the chain declares it, where before they
always set contract, even to "". A new test requires every pack formula
to parse with requires == {"formula_compiler": ">=2.0.0"} exactly, and
that exact comparison is what would catch a misplaced header.
Red-checked: it fails for all 34 files at origin/integration. The
assertions against third-party packs and the user-override fixtures still
use the alias and stay unchanged.

Docs: README.md, REQUIREMENTS.md and formulas/REQUIREMENTS.md now state
the [requires] rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
